  "design": "No new models, thresholds, policy variants or selection. Decompose the already-declared local pull advantage into avoided branch aggregate loss, forfeited branch aggregate gain and inventory-penalty reduction, exactly reconciling net utility. Separately value every sequential fill at its own price and physical fill time plus1s/5s using the same strict last-book age<=1000ms convention as generation marks. Match fills to generations by market/side/price/activation reconstructed from fill age; require unique identities and exact quantity/count/settlement/generation-mark reconciliation. Report positive/negative/zero value, missing marks and quantities by day/policy/scenario. Full portfolio paired comparisons remain the decision metric.",
  "controls": "Positive/negative/zero values; stale/invalid-book status and no future-row selection; valid fill-generation match and corrupted-age/ambiguous-generation refusal; exact component arithmetic and deliberately wrong decomposition refusal.",
  "limits": "Local branch gain/loss are signs of aggregate branch mark, not sums of favorable/adverse fills. Sequential fill profiles are descriptive conditional outcomes; they do not identify avoided fills across different policies. No fill-conditioned model fitting."
